  <%- include('./partials/nav') %>
  <div class="container-fluid p-3 info-container">
    <div class="intro">
      <h1 class="text-center">Play Dungeons and Dragons Online</h1>
      <p>
        Looking for a DnD group online? Browse active <strong>Public Wyrlds</strong>, request to join a campaign,
        and start playing with people who match your style. If you want to run games, you can also launch your own
        campaign as a DM or GM with tools built for long-term play. Far Reach Co. includes a fast browser-based
        <strong>virtual tabletop system</strong> plus <strong>Far Reach Radio</strong> for shared session music.
      </p>
      <small>
        <a href="/wyrlds/public">Browse Public Wyrlds</a>
        |
        <a href="/register">Create Free Account</a>
      </small>
      <hr>
    </div>

    <div class="quick-links" aria-label="Page sections">
      <a href="#find-games">Find Games</a>
      <a href="#join-campaigns">Join Campaigns</a>
      <a href="#new-players">New Players</a>
      <a href="#become-dm">Become a DM/GM</a>
      <a href="#tools">Tools</a>
      <a href="#start-now">Start Now</a>
    </div>

    <section id="find-games">
      <h2>Find Online DnD Games and Campaigns</h2>
      <p>
        A <strong>Wyrld</strong> is a persistent campaign hub: the GM's home base for that game, including table maps,
        lore records, onboarding notes, discussion threads, and linked character sheets. A <strong>Public Wyrld</strong>
        is simply a Wyrld that the GM chooses to list so new players can discover it and request to join.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Search Wyrlds by title and read campaign summaries.</li>
        <li>Check join mode: <strong>Request to Join</strong> or <strong>Invite Only</strong>.</li>
        <li>Review the featured onboarding record to understand tone and expectations.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Explore campaigns here: <a href="/wyrlds/public">Public Wyrld Directory</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="join-campaigns">
      <h2>How to Join a DnD Campaign Online</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Create a free account so you can send join requests.</li>
        <li>Browse listings and open campaigns that fit your schedule and play style.</li>
        <li>Send a short intro message when requesting to join.</li>
        <li>Wait for DM/GM approval and join the Wyrld when accepted.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        Need context first? Read the <a href="/public-wyrlds-guide">Public Wyrlds Guide</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="new-players">
      <h2>New to Online Tabletop RPGs?</h2>
      <p>
        If you are searching terms like <em>beginner DnD games</em>, <em>new player friendly DnD online</em>, or
        <em>DnD looking for group</em>, start with campaigns that clearly explain session cadence, table rules, and
        onboarding steps in their featured record.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Read campaign expectations before requesting to join.</li>
        <li>Mention your experience level and what style of game you enjoy.</li>
        <li>Start with one campaign and build consistency from there.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="become-dm">
      <h2>Want to Become a Game Master? Start Your Own Campaign</h2>
      <p>
        Players who want more control can become organizers. Create your own Wyrld, publish it in public discovery,
        and recruit players who are actively looking for online tabletop RPG games.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Create a Wyrld and set up campaign details.</li>
        <li>Enable public listing and choose your join mode.</li>
        <li>Add an onboarding record so players know exactly what to expect.</li>
        <li>Review incoming requests and build your party deliberately.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Setup help: <a href="/public-wyrlds-admin-guide">Public Wyrlds Admin Guide</a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="tools">
      <h2>Tools for Running Online games Successfully</h2>
      <p>
        Far Reach Co. is <strong>system-agnostic</strong> for tabletop RPG play, so you can run many TTRPG systems
        on the same virtual table. We currently provide our deepest built-in support for <strong>D&amp;D 5E</strong>.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Virtual tabletop system</strong> for maps, tokens, and shared play space.</li>
        <li><strong>Far Reach Radio</strong> for synced, table-wide audio atmosphere during sessions.</li>
        <li><strong>Records</strong> for lore, house rules, and campaign documentation.</li>
        <li><strong>Discussion threads</strong> for in-campaign coordination.</li>
        <li><strong>Linked character sheets</strong> with primary support for D&amp;D 5E campaigns.</li>
        <li><strong>Public listing controls</strong> to manage campaign visibility and intake.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Learn the platform: <a href="/what-is-frc">What is Far Reach Co?</a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="start-now">
      <div class="seo-cta-block">
        <p>Ready to play or run your own game?</p>
        <a class="seo-cta-primary" href="/register">Create Free Account</a>
        <a class="seo-cta-secondary" href="/wyrlds/public">Find Campaigns to Join</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
